{
  "case_id": "2018-17-532",
  "document_hash": "a79afbe9ce733faaa35d04508895f3f7859d9a80f9d27f39bb83939aae370146",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2018-17-532",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a79afbe9ce733faaa35d04508895f3f7859d9a80f9d27f39bb83939aae370146",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a79afbe9ce73-0000-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:11 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2018-17-532",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a79afbe9ce733faaa35d04508895f3f7859d9a80f9d27f39bb83939aae370146",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a79afbe9ce73-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. HICKS: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: In 1868, the Crow Tribe of Indians agreed to cede to the United States 30 million acres of its aboriginal land and move to a reservation. In exchange for ceding its land, the tribe expressly reserved the right to hunt on that ceded land. The text of the 1868 treaty memorializing this agreement explicitly identifies the four events that would cause the hunting right to terminate. Wyoming's admission to the Union is not among them. Therefore, the only way that Wyoming's statehood could have terminated the hunting right is by implication, but that is the very theory that this Court repeatedly rejected"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2018-17-532",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a79afbe9ce733faaa35d04508895f3f7859d9a80f9d27f39bb83939aae370146",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a79afbe9ce73-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: But --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Hicks",
      "case_id": "2018-17-532",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a79afbe9ce733faaa35d04508895f3f7859d9a80f9d27f39bb83939aae370146",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a79afbe9ce73-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, I certainly think that if it gives you heartburn to have two different results because you're applying your latest legal reasoning, I think you can take the extra step."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2018-17-532",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a79afbe9ce733faaa35d04508895f3f7859d9a80f9d27f39bb83939aae370146",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a79afbe9ce73-0001-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "that if -- if there are different results there, I think that's a consequence of the new reasoning that you set out in Mille Lacs."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Frederick Liu",
      "case_id": "2018-17-532",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a79afbe9ce733faaa35d04508895f3f7859d9a80f9d27f39bb83939aae370146",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a79afbe9ce73-0001-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If the principles of Mille Lacs apply here, I don't think there can be much doubt about the outcome. The decision below should be reversed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2018-17-532",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a79afbe9ce733faaa35d04508895f3f7859d9a80f9d27f39bb83939aae370146",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a79afbe9ce73-0001-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF FREDERICK LIU FOR THE UNITED STATES, AS AMICUS CURIAE, SUPPORTING THE PETITIONER"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-17-532",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a79afbe9ce733faaa35d04508895f3f7859d9a80f9d27f39bb83939aae370146",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a79afbe9ce73-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Would you please stop talking in generalities?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2018-17-532",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a79afbe9ce733faaa35d04508895f3f7859d9a80f9d27f39bb83939aae370146",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a79afbe9ce73-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Can I -- can we just --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-17-532",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a79afbe9ce733faaa35d04508895f3f7859d9a80f9d27f39bb83939aae370146",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a79afbe9ce73-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So tell me what in the treaty says it automatically terminates. I saw a lot of conditions. I saw the game disappearing, the land becoming occupied, but I don't see on statehood or even anything approaching it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2018-17-532",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a79afbe9ce733faaa35d04508895f3f7859d9a80f9d27f39bb83939aae370146",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a79afbe9ce73-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Can I ask about the practical consequences of the decision?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "State of Wyoming",
      "case_id": "2018-17-532",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a79afbe9ce733faaa35d04508895f3f7859d9a80f9d27f39bb83939aae370146",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a79afbe9ce73-0002-0006",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Conservation necessity is not a middle ground from the state's perspective, and the chief reason is because the law enforcement officers who act don't know whether they have jurisdiction until after they have done so."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2018-17-532",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a79afbe9ce733faaa35d04508895f3f7859d9a80f9d27f39bb83939aae370146",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a79afbe9ce73-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: On the land in question here, what is the extent of the federal government's regulatory authority and where does it come from?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2018-17-532",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a79afbe9ce733faaa35d04508895f3f7859d9a80f9d27f39bb83939aae370146",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a79afbe9ce73-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Does the government think that that abrogated the or that limited the treaty right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Knepper",
      "case_id": "2018-17-532",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a79afbe9ce733faaa35d04508895f3f7859d9a80f9d27f39bb83939aae370146",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a79afbe9ce73-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KNEPPER: The -- the federal government's regulatory authority comes from the Organic Act that created the national forests. There's a -- there's a gap. There was -- there was a statute allowing creation of the national forests. And then, when they were reaffirmed in 1897, the so-called Organic Act allows the federal government to just -- do just about anything. And in the Coastal California Commission, this Court said it's plenary."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Hicks",
      "case_id": "2018-17-532",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a79afbe9ce733faaa35d04508895f3f7859d9a80f9d27f39bb83939aae370146",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a79afbe9ce73-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. HICKS: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice. Just a few points. First, in response to the idea that Mille Lacs simply didn't change the approach, I -- I think that's wrong for all the reasons that Justice Breyer and Justice Kagan identified."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2018-17-532",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a79afbe9ce733faaa35d04508895f3f7859d9a80f9d27f39bb83939aae370146",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a79afbe9ce73-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted."
    },
    {
